# TOKEN ECONOMY (Layer 0)

Cross-cutting. Restricts **format**, not **content**. Quality (TDD, review, edge cases) > economy when conflict.

## 0.0 SUSPENSION GUARD — PLAN / gap-plan artifacts (AUTHORITATIVE)

**Trigger (any of):**
- Role command: `BACK PLAN`, `FRONT PLAN`, `INTEG PLAN`, `PM PLAN`, or any `* PLAN`
- Writing/updating: `memory-bank/**/plan-*.md`, `memory-bank/integration/gap/gap-*.md`, или gap closing plans `plan-BACK-GAP-*` / `plan-FRONT-GAP-*`

### FORBIDDEN while guard is active (plan/gap artifact OUTPUT)

- Apply §0.2 telegraph brevity to the plan file
- Cap size (~200 lines, «keep short», «оглавление достаточно»)
- Compress Element/API registry / omit routes or UI elements for length
- Treat chat «brief» as a reason to shorten `plan-*.md`
- Confuse lean **LOAD** (§0.3, §0.5.1) with lean **WRITE** of the plan

### REQUIRED

- Plan/gap artifact: **maximally detailed, exhaustive, comprehensive** — no line/size/brevity limits
- Chat with user MAY stay brief (1–3 sentences summary); **artifact must not**

### SUSPENDED for plan/gap artifact only

§0.2 · §0.5 size cap · §0.6 chunked execution · §0.12 single-pass economy · §0.15 session/chat economy **as applied to writing the plan file**

### RETAINED

§0.9 approval · §0.13 roles · §0.14 model routing · §0.10 session start / FINISH · lean **read** of unrelated shards (still don't dump whole memory-bank into context — but **do** inventory everything the PLAN workflow requires)

This section **supersedes** every conflicting brevity rule. Workflow PLAN files must restate it; if ignored → FAIL.

## 0.0.1 Load ≠ Write (Claude Code / Cursor)

| | Economy applies? | Notes |
|--|------------------|-------|
| **What you READ** into context | YES lean | `load_now`, ONE shard for IMPLEMENT; PLAN workflows may read **all portal-relevant** implement + routes as required by that workflow |
| **What you WRITE** to `plan-*.md` / `gap-*.md` | **NO lean** | §0.0 — full detail |
| **Chat reply to user** | YES brief OK | Do not mirror chat brevity into the plan file |

**Anti-pattern:** «Token economy → короткий plan». Correct: «Token economy → lean context load; plan file → maximal».

